: I've just written a simple program using DCE threads (it is my first !).
: Basically I want to create 2 threads which call a function to open a file
: The thread creation call is as follows :

:  if((pthread_create(&thread_hdl1, pthread_attr_default,
:             (pthread_startroutine_t) open_file,
:             (pthread_addr_t)NULL)) != 0)
:         {
:            fprintf(stderr,"%s\n","Unable to create thread1");
:            exit(1);
:         }

: where open-file is the function to open the file. The creation routine
: returns 0, which I assume is the valid value for a successful creation.
: However, the thread doesn't enter the function "open_file". I've stepped
: through the code with dbx and it just exits out of main. I've linked 
: with the thread-safe library libc_r.a
: Can someone please e-mail me as to what I might be doing wrong ?
: I am using DCE 1.2 threads on AIX 3.2.5 on an IBM PowerPC. 
