Yuh Ming YONG (ymyong@neumann.uwaterloo.ca) wrote:
: I notice that in DCE client's stub code the call handle is
: declared as having a volatile data type as follows:

: volatile rpc_call_handle_t call_h = NULL;


: Could anyone tell me the significant or meaning of volatile
: data type?  Thank you very much.

"volatile" is an ANSI C keyword that the RPC code uses in an attempt
to keep the C compiler from homing the variable in a register.  It
wants it not in a register since the variable is used along an
exception path--i.e., it may be reached by a call to longjmp() having
been made--and it doesn't trust the compiler (which is often not aware
of what longjmp() does to registers) to not mess things up.

--
                -- Nat Mishkin
                   Atria Software, Inc.
                   mishkin@atria.com


