In <781361999snz@vsfl.demon.co.uk> dave@vsfl.demon.co.uk writes:
>	I'm trying to find something on the net that can point me to
>	a list of standards/protocols that have been adopted by OSF's
>	DCE standard; along with a brief run down on each.

DCE NDR, the network data representation, is derived from (and
compatible with) the NDR used by Apollo's RPC system, NCS.  You
can get technical specs from the book Network Computing Architecture,
Zahn, et al ISBN 0-13-611674-4, by Prentice-Hall.

The threads is based on draft 4 of POSIX threads.

The security system uses Kerberos but over DCE RPC and in stylized ways.

The time service, cell directory service, and DFS are new protocols.
In some cases they are descended from other services, but they all
use DCE RPC now, so you can consider them to be new. 

The Global Directory Service is a full X.500 implementation.

OSF publishes standards-level documents that are available from OSF,
X/Open and Prentice-Hall, known as DCE AES documents.  RPC, Time,
and Directory are available now.

