1) The WIN-DFS Developer's Kit:

The UNIMETRIC WIN-DFS Developer's Kit supports the user-space
implementation of DFS clients running in the Window 3.1 environment.
The kit provides a complete set of POSIX-compliant filesystem function
calls for developers to develop Windows-based distributed applications
using DFS enhanced file services to share files on a LAN or WAN.  Data
is cached locally to improve performance, and strong consistency of the
cache is guaranteed.

Developers don't need to have in-depth knowledge of the DFS or DCE
protocols.  The Developer's Kit hides the underlying complexity of
programming with DFS.

Availability: end of '94


2) The SCO-DFS Developer's Kit:

The UNIMETRIC SCO-DFS Developer's Kit is a user-space implementation of 
DFS client software running in the Unix environment of SCO Open Desktop.

Developers don't need to have in-depth knowledge of the DFS protocols to 
develop distributed applications using DFS enhanced file services to share

files on a LAN or WAN. The Developer's Kit hides the underlying complexity

of programming with DFS.


Availability: end of '94


3) DFS-MAN on Win3.1

DFS-MAN is a Windows based File Manager-like application that
runs on out-of-the-box PC/DCE to allow end users to utilize DFS file
systems.  It supports moving and copying files and directories to and
from the PC client and DFS servers.  DFS-FMAN also supports creating
and deleting of local and remote directories.  It has a fully graphical
user interface for point-and-click browsing of DFS directory hierarchies

Availability: end of '94



