No, it's just the RPC and IDL that will be available without royalty
obligation. You will not have an entire DCE client. In fact, you won't
be able to write a secure RPC call. The motivation isn't to proliferate
DCE clients----OSF's action in that area was to lower the royalty fee
paid by implementors to $2/client regardless of volume where it once
ranged from $25 to $75/client depending on volume. This action was
directed at efforts to invent yet-another RPC mechanism as part of
CORBA 2.0 submission activities.

