In article <mauney.780683737@tophat.mauney.com>, mauney@tophat (Jon Mauney) says:
>
>Personally, I favor one of the alternate proposals:
>    comp.distributed
>which would likely have higher usage, since it would be a suitable home
>for DCE, CORBA, message-passing, etc, and could be subdivided
>at some point in the future, if necessary.  I think the distinction
>between "distributed" and "client-server" is enough to justify the
>new group, and I think that comp.client-server will not lack for
>continued traffic discussing Powerbuilder and the adequacy of the
>Gartner Group's C-S model.

My preference resonates with yours, i.e. that a single group be formed
to include DCE _and_ CORBA. (a similar discussion in comp.lang.idl is
currently taking place based on the erroneous assumption that it had
something to do with CORBA or DCE). My reasoning is that multiple groups
with narrow focus precludes the sharing of ideas between those using
different approaches for the construction of distributed systems.

I recognize that the potential for flame wars is greatly increased since
the inevetable "which is best?" question will be discussed. However, the
alternative (multiple more narrowly focused groups) means, at a minimum,
that I've got to scan more places, and at worst, that the quality of the
discussion will suffer.


