Here is how I back up a machine to a remote tape drive:

  rsh machine2 tar cf - / | dd ibs=4k obs=10k of=/dev/rmt0h

The key thing is that over a pipe, blocks are 4kb.  I have not tried
what you are wanting to do, but this is what I would try first:

  dd if=/dev/rmt2h ibs=10k obs=4k | rsh dec1 dd of=/dev/rmt0l ibs=4k obs=10k

I am no "dd" expert, but based on my experience, I see no reason why
it shouldn't work.  If you get it to work, I'd like to know what you
finally did - might be useful someday.

