It sounds like Yuh Ming is using automatic binding, and of course in that case 
the manager routines do not have access to the client binding handle. Note 
that the stubs should as a rule never be modified, and hence the 
rpc_binding_auth_inq() call should be made in the manager routines. In order 
to use this method you must be using explicit or implicit bindings. Note also 
that this does not work if you are using unauthenticated RPC. A principal name 
will only be returned by this call if the client has done a login and has 
authenticated it's server binding. 
